.TH SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SCALE_TO_DISPLAY 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SCALE_TO_DISPLAY \- A variable forcing non-DPI-aware Wayland windows to output at 1:1 scaling.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SCALE_TO_DISPLAY \(dqSDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SCALE_TO_DISPLAY\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This must be set before initializing the video subsystem\[char46]
.PP
When this hint is set, Wayland windows that are not flagged as being DPI-aware will be output with scaling designed to force 1:1 pixel mapping\[char46]
.PP
This is intended to allow legacy applications to be displayed without desktop scaling being applied, and has issues with certain display configurations, as this forces the window to behave in a way that Wayland desktops were not designed to accommodate:
.PP

\(bu Rounding errors can result with odd window sizes and/or desktop scales, which can cause the window contents to appear slightly blurry\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Positioning the window may be imprecise due to unit conversions and rounding\[char46]
.PP
\(bu The window may be unusably small on scaled desktops\[char46]
.PP
\(bu The window may jump in size when moving between displays of different scale factors\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Displays may appear to overlap when using a multi-monitor setup with scaling enabled\[char46]
.PP
\(bu Possible loss of cursor precision due to the logical size of the window being reduced\[char46]
.PP
New applications should be designed with proper DPI awareness handling instead of enabling this\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Windows will be scaled normally\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Windows will be forced to scale to achieve 1:1 output\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before creating a window\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

